<title>LEBANON: Solidere shares fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Solidere shares fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solidere shares fell on Monday on reduced turnover on the Beirut Stock Exchange (BSE).</p>
<p>A shares fell to $113 from Friday's $113.375 and B shares fell to $116.125 from $117. Turnover was 9,000 shares from 11,404 and value was $1,024,798.375 from $942,501 a day earlier.</p>
<p>Also traded on the market were 200 Eternit shares at $1.75 each, down from $1.8125 when they were last traded on November 21.</p>
<p>There was no trade in the three other companies listed on BSE: Ciments Libanais, Ciments Blancs and Uniceramic.</p>
<p>The LISPI stock index fell 0.65 percent to 82.90 and the BLOM stock index fell 0.47 percent to 967.13.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 353078 645456 602057</p>
</text>
